@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ocar-tests-fixtures`
IMPORT `ocar-11-12-cover`

-- TESTS for Articles 1.1, 2.1, 3.1.1, 11 and 12, and the supplementary clauses that move them.
-- Each exclusion has a fact pattern that triggers it and a near miss that does not; each peril
-- has a case inside the cover and one outside. Expected values are read from the source lines
-- cited beside them, never from an evaluation. A failing assertion here is a finding.

§ `Tests — cover and exclusions`

§§ `Fixtures for these tests`

GIVEN fs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance in a test`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a plain collision where` fs MEANS
    `a collision with` (`the circumstances with` fs) `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 10_000_000)

GIVEN `the certificate` IS A `The inspection certificate`
      fs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance in a test`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a collision with the inspection certificate` `the certificate` `, where` fs MEANS
    `a collision with` (`the circumstances, certificate` `the certificate` `, licence` `a valid licence appropriate to the vehicle` `, with` fs) `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 10_000_000)

GIVEN `the licence` IS A `The driving licence`
      fs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance in a test`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a collision with the driving licence` `the licence` `, where` fs MEANS
    `a collision with` (`the circumstances, certificate` `valid and in force` `, licence` `the licence` `, with` fs) `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 10_000_000)

GIVEN ls IS A `The load and speed`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a collision with the load` ls MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `by` `collision or impact, including with another object` `, circumstances` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, load` ls `, conduct` `good conduct` `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 10_000_000)

GIVEN l IS A `The loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `An exclusion in Article 12`
`the event exclusions on the plain policy for` l MEANS
    `12 — the exclusions of the event, on` `the plain policy` `for` l

GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
      i IS A `A damaged item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `An exclusion in Article 12`
`the item exclusions on` p `for a collision damaging` i MEANS
    `12 — the exclusions of the item, on` p `for` (`a collision with` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, items` (LIST i)) `:` i

`a goods vehicle` MEANS `a vehicle carrying` `goods` `, permitted load` 1000 `, permitted persons` 2

§§ `The plain case`

-- A sudden collision in Vietnam, in the period, nothing amiss: covered, nothing excluded.
#ASSERT `11 and 12 — the event is covered, on` `the plain policy` `for` `the plain collision`
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` `the plain collision` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `11 and 12 — the item is covered, on` `the plain policy` `for` `the plain collision` `:` (`a part repaired for` 10_000_000)

§§ `1.1, 2.1 and 3.1.1 — the policy in force for a motor car`

-- src:64-70: four or more wheels, not on rails, not a motorcycle.
`a three-wheeler` MEANS `The vehicle` WITH
    `number of wheels`                                          IS 3
    `runs on rails`                                             IS FALSE
    `a two- or three-wheeled motorcycle or a similar vehicle`   IS TRUE
    `origin`                                                    IS `manufactured in Vietnam`
    `new (100%) when insured`                                   IS FALSE
    `date of first registration in Vietnam`                     IS YMD 2022 3 15
    `year of manufacture`                                       IS 2022
    `use`                                                       IS `none of the uses listed in 14.1.2(b)`
    `carries`                                                   IS `goods`
    `permitted load in the inspection certificate`              IS 500
    `permitted number of persons in the inspection certificate` IS 2
#ASSERT `1.1 — a motor car within the definition` `the private car`
#ASSERT NOT `1.1 — a motor car within the definition` `a three-wheeler`
#ASSERT NOT `11 and 12 — the event is covered, on` (`a 2026 policy on` `a three-wheeler` `, concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, insured for` 100_000_000 `, market value` (JUST 100_000_000) `, with` EMPTY) `for` `the plain collision`

-- src:135-136: the period on the certificate, both ends included.
#ASSERT `2.1 — the date falls within the insurance period of` `the plain policy` `:` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`2.1 — the date falls within the insurance period of` `the plain policy` `:` (YMD 2027 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `11 and 12 — the event is covered, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `by` `collision or impact, including with another object` `, circumstances` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, load` `normal load` `, conduct` `good conduct` `, items` EMPTY)

-- src:162-166: premium not paid in full by 15 January 2026, no deferral: the contract ends that
-- day; a loss on 10 June is not covered. With a deferral agreed, it is.
`the policy with half the premium paid` MEANS `the plain policy with deductible` NOTHING `, reduction level` NOTHING `, premium paid` 6_000_000 `, owing allowed` FALSE `, other policies` EMPTY
`the policy with half the premium paid, deferral agreed` MEANS `the plain policy with deductible` NOTHING `, reduction level` NOTHING `, premium paid` 6_000_000 `, owing allowed` TRUE `, other policies` EMPTY
#ASSERT `3.1.1 — the date the contract terminates for late premium` `the policy with half the premium paid` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `11 and 12 — the event is covered, on` `the policy with half the premium paid` `for` `the plain collision`
#ASSERT `11 and 12 — the event is covered, on` `the policy with half the premium paid, deferral agreed` `for` `the plain collision`

§§ `11.1 — the perils`

-- src:566-574: each peril the five bullets list is covered; another cause is not.
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `collision or impact, including with another object` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `overturning` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `tipping over` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `sinking` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `the whole vehicle falling` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `being struck by a falling object` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `conflagration, fire or explosion` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `a natural catastrophe` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `theft or robbery of the whole vehicle` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `a malicious act or deliberate destruction` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `some other cause` `, items` EMPTY)

-- src:572-574: a malicious act by the Policyholder, the Insured, the Owner, the Driver or an
-- interested person is outside bullet 5.
#ASSERT NOT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `by` `a malicious act or deliberate destruction` `, circumstances` (`the circumstances with` (LIST `fact 11.1 the malicious act was by an interested person`)) `, load` `normal load` `, conduct` `good conduct` `, items` EMPTY)

-- src:553-554: the event must be sudden and unforeseeable (fork F17: not asked of a natural
-- catastrophe, which is itself "thiên tai").
`a foreseeable collision` MEANS `The loss` WITH
    `date of the loss`                                          IS YMD 2026 6 10
    `peril`                                                     IS `collision or impact, including with another object`
    `sudden and unforeseeable`                                  IS FALSE
    `circumstances`                                             IS `the circumstances with` EMPTY
    `load and speed`                                            IS `normal load`
    `conduct`                                                   IS `good conduct`
    `items`                                                     IS EMPTY
    `share of the painted area damaged`                         IS 0
    `cost of repainting the damaged panels`                     IS 0
    `cost of repainting the whole vehicle`                      IS 0
    `cost of protecting the scene and preventing further loss`  IS 0
    `cost of rescue and transport to the nearest repair shop`   IS 0
    `the costs were incurred at the Insurer's request and direction` IS FALSE
    `market value immediately before the loss`                  IS 600_000_000
    `assessed damage`                                           IS 0
    `assessed cost of repair`                                   IS 0
    `a court judgment, or a decision to suspend the investigation or not to prosecute` IS FALSE
    `the Owner asks to keep the wreck`                          IS FALSE
    `value of the wreck, as valued`                             IS 0
#ASSERT NOT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` `a foreseeable collision`

-- BS03 (src:1051-1053) and BS05 (src:1082-1085) add a peril only where the clause is in effect,
-- its premium paid in full and on time (Article 12 chapeau, src:588-590).
`the policy with BS03` MEANS `the 2026 policy with` (LIST `clause accepted and paid in full and on time:` `BS03 flood damage`)
`the policy with BS03 paid late` MEANS `the 2026 policy with` (LIST `clause accepted and paid in full but late:` `BS03 flood damage`)
`the policy with BS05` MEANS `the 2026 policy with` (LIST `clause accepted and paid in full and on time:` `BS05 loss of parts`)
#ASSERT NOT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `driving into flood water` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT     `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the policy with BS03` `for` (`a loss by` `driving into flood water` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the policy with BS03 paid late` `for` (`a loss by` `driving into flood water` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `theft or robbery of parts` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT     `11.1 — the peril is one the cover lists, on` `the policy with BS05` `for` (`a loss by` `theft or robbery of parts` `, items` EMPTY)

§§ `Article 12 — exclusions that describe the event: each triggered, each missed`

-- 12.1, src:593-595.
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a plain collision where` (LIST `fact 12.1 deliberately caused`)) EQUALS LIST `12.1 deliberate act`
#ASSERT `11 and 12 — the event is covered, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `a malicious act or deliberate destruction` `, items` EMPTY)

-- 12.2, src:596-605: in traffic without a valid certificate; not when parked; not when it
-- lapsed only for one of the bracketed reasons; (iii) only if no more persons than permitted.
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the inspection certificate` `missing, invalid, expired or not conforming` `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS LIST `12.2 no valid inspection certificate`
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the inspection certificate` `missing, invalid, expired or not conforming` `, where` (LIST `fact not in traffic`)) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the inspection certificate` `lapsed only because tyres or rims were changed within the maker's specification` `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the inspection certificate` `lapsed only because protective fittings, a roof rack, a winch or a tow hook were added` `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the inspection certificate` `lapsed only because seats were added` `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `12.2 — applies to` `the private car` `and` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `by` `collision or impact, including with another object` `, circumstances` (`the circumstances, certificate` `lapsed only because seats were added` `, licence` `a valid licence appropriate to the vehicle` `, with` EMPTY) `, load` (`carrying` 0 `, persons counting children` 6 `, not counting them` 6 `, speed over the limit` NOTHING) `, conduct` `good conduct` `, items` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `12.2 — applies to` `the private car` `and` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `by` `collision or impact, including with another object` `, circumstances` (`the circumstances, certificate` `lapsed only because seats were added` `, licence` `a valid licence appropriate to the vehicle` `, with` EMPTY) `, load` (`carrying` 0 `, persons counting children` 5 `, not counting them` 5 `, speed over the limit` NOTHING) `, conduct` `good conduct` `, items` EMPTY)

-- 12.3, src:616-621: no licence, or one withdrawn, lost or held past the appointment, for a
-- vehicle that needs one, in traffic.
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the driving licence` `no licence` `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS LIST `12.3 no valid driving licence`
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the driving licence` `a licence withdrawn, lost, or held by the police past the appointment` `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS LIST `12.3 no valid driving licence`
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the driving licence` `a licence that is invalid or not appropriate to the vehicle` `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS LIST `12.3 no valid driving licence`
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the driving licence` `no licence` `, where` (LIST `fact 12.3 no licence is required`)) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the event exclusions on the plain policy for` (`a collision with the driving licence` `no licence` `, where` (LIST `fact not in traffic`)) EQUALS EMPTY

